1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,160
It's six forty-five

2
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:01,950
in the morning.

3
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:03,570
Marco just called in sick.

4
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,650
Four customers are waiting

5
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:05,640
for him today.

6
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:07,120
Who covers his jobs?

7
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:07,850
Figuring that out

8
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:09,330
by hand takes an hour.

9
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:10,180
Second Shift does it

10
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:11,210
in seconds.

11
00:00:12,425 --> 00:00:13,525
Someone posts in Slack:

12
00:00:13,535 --> 00:00:14,645
Marco is out.

13
00:00:14,655 --> 00:00:15,775
Second Shift reads it,

14
00:00:15,785 --> 00:00:16,845
then looks at every job

15
00:00:16,855 --> 00:00:18,065
and every calendar.

16
00:00:18,404 --> 00:00:19,584
It builds a new plan.

17
00:00:19,594 --> 00:00:21,034
Watch the trucks move.

18
00:00:21,044 --> 00:00:21,904
Wei can do Marco's

19
00:00:21,914 --> 00:00:22,624
big gas job,

20
00:00:22,634 --> 00:00:23,794
but he's busy.

21
00:00:23,804 --> 00:00:24,454
So Ana takes

22
00:00:24,464 --> 00:00:25,414
Wei's small job,

23
00:00:25,424 --> 00:00:26,944
and Wei takes Marco's.

24
00:00:26,954 --> 00:00:27,614
One job can't

25
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:28,494
be saved today,

26
00:00:28,504 --> 00:00:29,524
so that customer is asked

27
00:00:29,534 --> 00:00:30,714
to pick a new time.

28
00:00:31,141 --> 00:00:32,181
Nothing changes until

29
00:00:32,191 --> 00:00:33,661
a person says yes.

30
00:00:33,671 --> 00:00:34,311
One click,

31
00:00:34,321 --> 00:00:35,641
and it updates the calendars

32
00:00:35,651 --> 00:00:36,551
and the job sheet,

33
00:00:36,561 --> 00:00:37,931
messages the team in Slack,

34
00:00:37,941 --> 00:00:39,531
and emails the customers.

35
00:00:39,914 --> 00:00:41,674
Then it double-checks every change.

36
00:00:41,684 --> 00:00:43,524
Thirty-six out of thirty-six.

37
00:00:43,534 --> 00:00:44,724
If it crashes halfway,

38
00:00:44,734 --> 00:00:45,234
it finishes

39
00:00:45,244 --> 00:00:47,054
without sending anything twice.

40
00:00:47,064 --> 00:00:47,864
And you can ask:

41
00:00:47,874 --> 00:00:48,334
what if Wei

42
00:00:48,344 --> 00:00:49,424
doesn't show up?

43
00:00:49,434 --> 00:00:50,024
It shows you,

44
00:00:50,034 --> 00:00:51,304
before it happens.

45
00:00:51,674 --> 00:00:52,274
Sick days,

46
00:00:52,284 --> 00:00:54,094
flat tires, no-shows.

47
00:00:54,104 --> 00:00:55,414
They'll keep happening.

48
00:00:55,424 --> 00:00:56,324
Now they take seconds

49
00:00:56,334 --> 00:00:57,074
to fix,

50
00:00:57,084 --> 00:00:57,994
not an hour.

51
00:00:58,004 --> 00:00:59,234
We can't predict the day.

52
00:00:59,244 --> 00:01:00,014
But we can be ready

53
00:01:00,024 --> 00:01:00,794
for it.

54
00:01:00,804 --> 00:01:01,874
Second Shift.

